# GitHub Terrain — a WebGPU (react-native-webgpu) instanced-cube render of a GitHub
# contribution calendar: tapping springs between the flat grid and a 3D isometric
# terrain, the switch springs between real and generated data; the JS render
# loop stops when both springs settle and restarts on demand.
# What this test covers: flat -> 3D -> flat with full settles; the data
# switch both ways in each view; tapping again mid-spring (retarget, loop
# already running); toggling the switch mid-view-spring; a rapid tap burst;
# and closing/reopening the demo quickly so WebGPU init (50ms timeout +
# async adapter/device) races the unmount cleanup.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/github-terrain"
wait "label=\"Toggle real GitHub contribution data\"" 10000
wait 3500
press 201 437
wait 2000
press "label=\"Toggle real GitHub contribution data\""
wait 2000
press 201 437
wait 2000
press "label=\"Toggle real GitHub contribution data\""
wait 2000
# Retarget mid-spring and switch mid-spring.
press 201 437
wait 250
press 201 437
wait 250
press "label=\"Toggle real GitHub contribution data\""
wait 250
press 201 437
wait 2500
press "label=\"Toggle real GitHub contribution data\""
wait 1500
# Rapid burst.
press 201 437 --count 7 --interval-ms 80
wait 2500
# Close and reopen quickly (init vs cleanup race).
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
open "demos://animations/github-terrain"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 3000
press 201 437
wait 2500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
